title: The May Cabinet Crisis
subtitle: The Kadets, the Soviet and the Allies.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dix >= 9 and in_coalition = 1 and gov_kadets = 1 and may_crisis_seen = 0
priority: 5
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: may_crisis_seen = 1;

= The Cabinet in Crisis

The Kadet ministers and the Soviet's ministers disagree about everything: the land, the eight-hour day, the army committees, the date of the Constituent Assembly. The Kadets have begun to talk about resignation. Tsereteli and Skobelev seek the middle ground, and the Internationalists in the party say that the compromise is a surrender.

- @keep: Keep the cabinet together, whatever the price.
- @no_kadets: Move toward a government of the Soviet parties alone.

@keep
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 4, rel_sr: -2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 6);
!}

The cabinet holds. The party's ministers have given up more than the Kadets did.

@no_kadets
choose-if: rel_sr >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: The SRs will not agree to this.
on-arrival: {!
Q.gov_kadets = 0;
Q.homogeneous_gov = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: -12, right_threat: 6, soviet_democracy: 2, ruble: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2, soldiers: 2, middle: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 3, -4);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -2, 5);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 6);
!}

The Kadets have left the government. What remains is a cabinet of the Soviet parties, and nobody to blame.
